      "message": "test(app): the workholding rpm table asserts all 24 cells\n\nThe walk in every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict\nasserted 15 of its 24 cells. The 9 it skipped are the creation refusals:\nturning work on a mill (none/mill x Work) and milling work on a plain\nlathe (lathe x Tool). Each is now asserted refused at creation, by its\nmessage; every other cell must be created and judged as before.\n\nA new pin reaches the work_speed arm for a milling section on a plain\nlathe through program_problems_by: over the chuck it is named, at the\nlimit it is clean. Through post() the family clause refuses it first.\nNo product code changes.\n\nFixes #1215\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
